To use the Virtual Fly Brain Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool, follow these steps:
Open Claude Desktop and go to Settings, navigate to the MCP section, add a new MCP server with the settings:
Server Name: virtual-fly-brain,
Type: HTTP,
Server URL: https://vfb3-mcp.virtualflybrain.org.
Alternatively, use the Configuration JSON or locate your Claude configuration file and add the VFB3-MCP server to your configuration.
For GitHub Copilot, open VS Code with GitHub Copilot installed, open Settings, search for "MCP" in the settings search, find the MCP Servers setting, add the server URL, and give it a name like "Virtual Fly Brain".
For other MCP-compatible clients, use the provided JSON configuration.
Once configured, test the connection by asking your AI assistant questions like "Get information about the neuron " or "Search for terms related to medulla in the fly brain".

```
{
"mcpServers": {
"virtual-fly-brain": {
"type": "http",
"url": "https://vfb3-mcp.virtualflybrain.org",
"tools": ["*"]
}
}
}
```
